
  Next fork, and it's the one with lasting consequences.

  [1mThe fork:[0m [38;5;153mapp.js[39m is loaded as a plain [38;5;153m<script>[39m, so it has no [38;5;153mimport[39m. [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m are CommonJS, which
  browsers can't load at all. A shared validation module has to be reachable from both the page and (if you want tests)
  Node — and the three ways to do that differ in what you're locked into later, not just in syntax.

  - [1mES modules[0m — [38;5;153msrc/validation.mjs[39m uses [38;5;153mexport[39m; [38;5;153mindex.html[39m becomes [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m. Browser-native,
    no build step, and Node can [38;5;153mimport[39m the same file for tests. Cost: module scripts are blocked over [38;5;153mfile://[39m by CORS,
    so opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m by double-clicking stops working — you'd need [38;5;153mnpx serve[39m or similar. Hard to walk back cheaply
    once other forms import it.
  - [1mGlobal script[0m — [38;5;153msrc/validation.js[39m attaches to [38;5;153mwindow[39m; add a second [38;5;153m<script>[39m tag before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m. Zero friction, still
    works over [38;5;153mfile://[39m. Cost: no import graph, and unit-testing it in Node needs a shim. Cheap to migrate to ESM later
    while there's one consumer; progressively less cheap as forms are added.
  - [1mDual export (UMD-ish)[0m — one file that works as both a browser global and a CommonJS [38;5;153mrequire[39m. Buys both without
    choosing. Cost: boilerplate wrapper around a ~30-line module, and it's a pattern the rest of this repo doesn't use.

  [1mMy recommendation: ES modules.[0m It's the only one of the three that makes the module testable in Node without a shim,
  and since "future-proofing" is the actual goal here, the import graph is the part that pays off when forms two and
  three arrive. The [38;5;153mfile://[39m regression is the real cost and I don't want to hide it — if you open [38;5;153mindex.html[39m directly
  rather than through a server, that alone should decide it for the global script.
